**Definition 5.1 (initial weak frame).** To specify the initial optimal
family, write

$$
\begin{gathered}
q(t)=\sqrt{\alpha+\beta t^2},\quad
D(t)=1+\alpha+(1+\beta)t^2,\quad
\psi(t)=\frac{(q(t),-1,-t)G(q(t),-1,-t)^T}{D(t)},\\
\mathcal A(t)=\alpha[\beta-(1+\beta)t^2],\quad
\mathcal B(t)=\beta[\alpha t^2-(1+\alpha)],\\
k(t)=\frac{\mathcal B(t)}{t+\sqrt{t^2-\mathcal A(t)\mathcal B(t)}},
\quad p(t)=\sqrt{\alpha+\beta k(t)^2},\\
f_0(t)=\frac{(q(t),-1,-t)^T}{\sqrt{D(t)}},\quad
f_1(t)=\frac{(p(t),1,k(t))^T}{\sqrt{D(k(t))}},\quad
f_2(t)=f_0(t)\times f_1(t),\quad
h(t)=\frac{2p(t)}{D(k(t))}.
\end{gathered}
\tag{TA.28}
$$

JR50 selects the unique stationary $t_*\in(17/20,9/10)$ of $\psi$.
JR54 and RC63 supply the orthonormal real-null frame above for
$t_*\leq t\leq t_\dagger$, its positive radicals and denominators,
$k(t)<0$, $tp(t)+q(t)k(t)>0$, and increasing $h$. Its height signs
are $(-,+,+)$ and maximizing reports $(-,+,-)$. Put
$\bar s=s_0h(t_*)$. For $s\leq\bar s$ the fixed $t_*$ frame
is height-optimal and satisfies the contrast inequality. For
$\bar s<s\leq s_\dagger=s_0h(t_\dagger)$ take the unique
$h(t)=s/s_0$. The height values are respectively
$T_{\rm flat}-\psi(t_*)$ and $T_{\rm flat}-\psi(t)$.
Plateau equality fixes the same three rays, even when the report
assignment has slack. These are credited JR/RH statements.

